{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Vaspertil","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/vaspertil.webp","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/vaspertil.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Vaspertil","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":180,"temp":0,"max":180,"details":""},"ac":{"value":30,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":40,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":"freedom of movement"},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":10,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["chthonian","draconic","empyrean","requian"],"details":"can't speak any language, telepathy 100 feet"},"level":{"value":10},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Vaspertil are mirrors of potential, a clean slate: demons who decided to follow a path of redemption. Whether through summons or of their own volition, vaspertil seek out those who pride themselves on their powers and talents and force them to question what really defines them.</p>\n<p>While atoning for their fiendish nature has left vaspertils faceless and mutilated, dismissing their abyssal roots has also introduced a sense of appreciation to their existence, one that is usually only acquired by the loss of something previously taken for granted.</p>\n<p>Despite being telepathic, vaspertils almost exclusively communicate through body language.</p>\n<h2>Til We Meet Again</h2>\n<p>Vaspertils consider their battles to be tests of their foes. Those able to defeat a vaspertil in fair combat earn its respect and a boon appropriate to vaspertil philosophy. They may be willing to join a quest that confronts an adventurer's fears or provide information against abyssal threats. Vaspertils won't fight people's battles for them but are willing to help them supplement and overcome their weaknesses.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 125/275/500 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Religion, Society, Stealth, Survival)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, chaotic, darkness, dexterity, energy resistant (negative), spells (Occult: darkness, dimension door, freedom of movement, nondetection), strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Julian Röth","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":7},"dex":{"mod":7},"con":{"mod":3},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":5},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":19,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":16,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"